From 86fb2b1e45df20ac9a02dc9b1f41caaffe73ecc7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 19:15:23 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] White-label: contrast-safe icons + fix hard-coded white
 surfaces app-wide

Icons (dashboard quick actions, setup checklist, and every page): add
contrast-safe iconColor/iconBg tokens to useTheme and useClientTheme. The
token equals the brand primary unless it is too close in luminance to the
card (the wash-out case), where it shifts toward black/white so icons stay
on-brand but readable. Swapped icon glyphs and dashboard badge fills over.

White-label surfaces: card/panel/field backgrounds that hard-coded #ffffff
in light mode now follow the (possibly customized) card/input colors, on the
marketing, outreach, settings, team, leads, templates and client-level pages
(client input token included), so an agency's palette drives every surface.

Branding: give each color group (Sidebar/Navigation, Page, Cards, Text,
Buttons) its own Save Changes button.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UPzvV8ByiAsVsK7osibmBQ
